🔴 STRATEGIC FINDING (banked 2026-05-30): Q2 surface is 70+ models app-wide — purchasing was a 9-model slice.
Full-schema grep during Batch 32 pre-flight revealed the tenant isolation gap extends far beyond purchasing.
Rough categories (all `@@schema("public")` + no tenantId — verified by grep):
  - Catalog:     Product, ProductSerialNumber, Category, ProductPurchaseHistory, Warehouse, WarehouseStock, StockMovement
  - HR:          Employee, AttendanceRecord, LeaveRequest, CashAdvance, CashAdvanceRecovery, Payroll, Payslip
  - Accounting:  Account, JournalEntry, JournalLine, TaxRate, FiscalYear, Expense, ExpenseCategory
  - Projects:    Project, ProjectExpense, ProjectNote, Milestone, TimeLog, Task, TaskAssignment, ToDo
  - CRM:         Customer, CustomerContact, CustomerCreditAccount, CustomerCreditTransaction, Proposal, Quotation
  - POS:         POSSession, POSSale, POSSaleItem
  - Support:     SupportTicket, TicketComment
  - Job Orders:  JobOrder, JobOrderPart, JobOrderServiceLine
  - Finance:     FundSource, FundTransaction, FundTransfer, FundRequest, CreditCardTransaction, CreditCardPayment, Invoice, Payment, Subscription
System tables (Tenant, Plan, User, Role, AuditLog) are intentionally tenant-agnostic — correct as-is.
All others above are Q2 business data lacking isolation. Tests pass only because fixtures don't exercise
cross-tenant access. Recommend treating as Direction L (multi-batch, module-by-module) when dev is further along.

